<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Delian League</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">478–<a href="/years/404-bce">404 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Delian League was an alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-city-states">Greek city-states</a> founded in 478 BCE under Athenian leadership to continue the war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, with its treasury first on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delos">Delos</a>. Members contributed ships or money, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> gradually turned the league into an empire, moving the treasury to Athens in 454 BCE. It was dissolved after Athens' defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a> in 404 BCE.</p></div>
